update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='c) identifying a person(s), authorized by an appropriate level of management, to work with the respective management representatives in support of water efficiency activities; | The management representative may be a current or contracted individual. The responsibilities of the management representative may represent all or part of the job function. Skills and competencies may be determined with respect to an organization’s size, culture and complexity, or to legal or other requirements. — printed p.10, 23', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§5.3 c); A.6, printed p.10, 23) [VA — PDF text layer] — CAVEAT: §5.3 c) obliges assigning a person(s); the term "management representative" and its flexibility come from A.6, which is INFORMATIVE and modal ("may") — the field is therefore correctly is_required=false', verified_at=now() where id='5b07c642-9838-4225-b725-711602bf8e2a' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- ---------------- ISO-46001-03 — Planung: Risiken, Chancen & Ziele ----------------
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_008 — Nachweis: 6.1
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='When planning for the water efficiency management system, the organization shall consider the issues referred to in 4.1 and the requirements referred to in 4.2 b), and determine the risks and opportunities that need to be addressed to: a) give assurance that the water efficiency management system can achieve its intended outcome(s); b) prevent, or reduce, undesired effects; c) achieve continual improvement; d) forecast related short-, mid- and long-term economic and investment impacts; | e) allocate necessary human and financial resources. The organization shall plan: 1) actions to address these risks and opportunities; 2) how to: — integrate and implement the actions into its water efficiency management system processes; — evaluate the effectiveness of these actions; — establish mid- and long-term projections, and allocate human and financial resources accordingly; — foster financial, technical or administrative innovation to control risks. The organization shall maintain documented information on: i. risks and opportunities; ii. the process(es) and actions needed to determine and address its risks and opportunities to the extent necessary to have confidence that they are carried out as planned. — printed p.10-11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.1, printed p.10-11) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-008 (clause 6.1)', verified_at=now() where id='4a24d1e4-6374-40f8-b1f8-b16b0fba8347' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_009 — Nachweis: 6.2.1
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization shall establish water efficiency objectives at relevant functions and levels. The water efficiency objectives shall: a) be consistent with the water efficiency policy; b) be measurable (if practicable); c) take into account applicable requirements; d) be monitored; e) be communicated; f) be updated as appropriate (for example following internal or external benchmarking). The organization shall retain documented information on the water efficiency objectives. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.1, printed p.11) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-009 (clause 6.2.1)', verified_at=now() where id='ecce35e9-f00e-4a6d-8ac3-9a3fd04a9fc1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_010 — Nachweis: 6.2.1
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='When planning how to achieve its water efficiency objectives, the organization shall determine: 1) what will be done; 2) what resources will be required; 3) who will be responsible; 4) when it will be completed; 5) how the results will be evaluated. — printed p.11', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.1 1)-5), printed p.11) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-010 (clause 6.2.1)', verified_at=now() where id='886dfa5e-755d-43c9-9296-0ff9fe839a21' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_012 — Nachweis: 6.2.2
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization shall implement and document its water efficiency planning process(es). | A water efficiency management plan is a document detailing the following: a) identification of locations/areas of an organization’s current water use; b) identification of water recycling potential in the organization’s processes and measurement of quantity and quality of water before and after for those processes that have been identified as having water recycling/recovery potential; c) identification of water-saving measures that can be readily applied, with links to the respective management systems and processes; d) an action plan to implement the identified measures, including identified savings, programme priority and implementation timelines. — printed p.11-12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.2, printed p.11-12) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-012 (clause 6.2.2). DUPLICATE/SUPERSET: gate CR-011 (planning_process_documented) blocks on the very same first sentence of §6.2.2 — staged', verified_at=now() where id='2d66d76b-38c8-483a-8804-f8a602bff8df' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_013 — Nachweis: 6.2.3
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization shall ensure that legal requirements or other requirements are considered in establishing, implementing and maintaining the water efficiency management system and are reviewed at defined intervals. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.3, printed p.12) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-013 (clause 6.2.3)', verified_at=now() where id='7ce98d5c-c8f2-4b8e-ac6a-d75c6935587d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_014 — Nachweis: 6.2.4
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization shall develop, conduct and maintain a water use review to: a) identify the activities and functions that use water; b) record the water used for each identified activity and function; c) determine processes and services that affect the used water quality, with the aim of segregating the used water streams with the objective of water recycling; d) determine activities and functions with the potential for greater water efficiency. | The methodology and criteria used to develop the water use review shall be maintained as documented information. — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.4, printed p.12) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-014 (clause 6.2.4). MIS-HOMED: gate on ws-03, the §6.2.4 fields are on ws-04 — staged', verified_at=now() where id='d1499eef-f570-4ffe-8fb8-997160ae720a' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_015 — Nachweis: 6.2.4
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='To develop the water use review, the organization shall: 1) analyse water use based on measurement and other data as follows: — identify current water sources; — identify current water-using activities and functions; — evaluate past and present water use; — estimate future water use. | 2) identify, based on the water use analysis, the activities and functions of significant water use, including: — the facilities, equipment, systems, processes and personnel working for or on behalf of the organization that significantly affect water use; — printed p.12', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.4 1)-2), printed p.12) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-015 (clause 6.2.4). The gate source_quote starts at "identify, based on..." and drops the governing lead-in "To develop the water use review, the organization shall:", so no "shall" is on the face of that quote — restored here. MIS-HOMED: gate on ws-03, fields on ws-04 — staged', verified_at=now() where id='184437eb-b84f-4707-8a2f-564a6d601b1c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-03 · attest_iso_46001_03_cr_016 — Nachweis: 6.2.5
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization shall identify specific business activity indicator(s) appropriate for monitoring and measuring water efficiency performance. The methodology for determining and updating the business activity indicator(s) shall be retained as documented information, regularly reviewed and periodically updated as appropriate. Annex D gives examples of business activity indicator(s). — printed p.13', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (§6.2.5, printed p.13) [VA — PDF text layer] — attestation checkbox for gate CR-016 (clause 6.2.5). MIS-HOMED: gate on ws-03, business_activity_indicator is on ws-04 — staged', verified_at=now() where id='34ff309d-9b8d-48df-b42e-7b51e019695d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
