-- ISO-46001-08 · O1 — Wasserausgang 1
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Water output to be included in a water balance chart consists of types and quantities of: 1) water that is lost through evaporation and drift from the facility, for example cooling towers; 2) water that is contained in the facility’s products, for example beverage; 3) water use for irrigation; 4) used water discharged from the facility into the sewer system, which includes foul wastewater and effluent from any on-site wastewater treatment facility; 5) water lost through leaking assets, including piping systems and ancillary infrastructure, or water used for general property and facility cleaning processes. | The water balance can be computed using Formula (C.2). Win = Wout WD + R1 + R2 + R3 = O1 + O2 + O3 + O4 — printed p.33-34', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (Annex C; Formula (C.2), printed p.33-34) [VA — PDF text layer] — CAVEAT: the printed water-output list has FIVE items 1)-5) while Formula (C.2) carries only FOUR O-terms; those four come from the Figure C.1 worked example, not from the generic list. O1 is not individually defined in the text', verified_at=now() where id='a013ba4b-e8c6-4fce-a294-08ededd90c5e' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
