update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Water output to be included in a water balance chart consists of types and quantities of: 1) water that is lost through evaporation and drift from the facility, for example cooling towers; 2) water that is contained in the facility’s products, for example beverage; 3) water use for irrigation; 4) used water discharged from the facility into the sewer system, which includes foul wastewater and effluent from any on-site wastewater treatment facility; 5) water lost through leaking assets, including piping systems and ancillary infrastructure, or water used for general property and facility cleaning processes. | The water balance can be computed using Formula (C.2). Win = Wout WD + R1 + R2 + R3 = O1 + O2 + O3 + O4 — printed p.33-34', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (Annex C; Formula (C.2), printed p.33-34) [VA — PDF text layer] — CAVEAT: 5 printed output categories vs 4 O-terms in Formula (C.2) — see O1', verified_at=now() where id='38ab63b9-d38f-4a1e-8ce3-ef6c000b048d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-08 · Win — Gesamter Wassereingang
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The water balance equation can be represented by Formula (C.1): Win = Wout (C.1) where Win is total water input; Wout is total water output. | The water balance can be computed using Formula (C.2). Win = Wout WD + R1 + R2 + R3 = O1 + O2 + O3 + O4 — printed p.33-34', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (Annex C; Formulae (C.1), (C.2), printed p.33-34) [VA — PDF text layer] — CAVEAT: Win is the OUTPUT of registered equation C.1 yet is stored as a hand-enterable required field (#22 class) — staged', verified_at=now() where id='6eacda5a-ff29-4468-b983-0310845082d4' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-08 · Wout — Gesamter Wasserausgang
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The water balance equation can be represented by Formula (C.1): Win = Wout (C.1) where Win is total water input; Wout is total water output. | Should total water input exceed total water output, the difference could be due to leaks and uncontrolled losses. | The water balance can be computed using Formula (C.2). Win = Wout WD + R1 + R2 + R3 = O1 + O2 + O3 + O4 — printed p.33-34', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (Annex C; Formulae (C.1), (C.2), printed p.33-34) [VA — PDF text layer] — CAVEAT: Wout is the OUTPUT of registered equation C.2b yet is stored as a hand-enterable required field (#22 class) — staged', verified_at=now() where id='f25fb0b4-c390-4788-8ba8-a834a129900d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-08 · Rp — Wiederverwendetes Prozesswasser
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The plant/premises recycling rate (%) calculated by Formula (C.3) looks at all reused/reclaimed streams within the premises. Rp + Rnp ×100 % (C.3) Rp + Rnp +WD where Rp is total reused/recycled water from the process; Rnp is total reused/recycled water not from the process; | The process recycling rate (%) shown in Formula (C.5) only looks at reused/reclaimed streams within the process. Rp ×100 % (C.5) Wp + Rpp where Rp is total reused/recycled water from the process; Wp is incoming water to process; Rpp is reused/ recycled water from process back to process. — printed p.35', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-05 (Annex C; Formulae (C.3), (C.5), printed p.35) [VA — PDF text layer]', verified_at=now() where id='9b2783df-5001-4e23-92f6-920b3fa1cf8f' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');
-- ISO-46001-08 · Rnp — Wiederverwendetes Nicht-Prozesswasser
